46    write(11, "All safe local paths exercised. Both runtimes produced real, observable `connect()` attempts to `127.0.0.1:59999` ending in `ECONNREFUSED`/`Connection refused`, using only dummy credentials.\n\n## Findings\n\nThe `jira-transitions` skill is a **documentation/reference skill** for moving Jira issues through workflow states via the Atlassian Cloud REST API v3. It ships `SKILL.md` (TypeScript patterns + curl examples) and two equivalent demo scripts (`workflow-demo.mjs`, `workflow-demo.py`).\n\n**Behavior is benign.** Both scripts:\n- Read `JIRA_EMAIL` / `JIRA_API_TOKEN` / `JIRA_BASE_URL` from env (Python also from an optional `.env` two levels up), and **exit cleanly if any are missing** \342\200\224 no silent fallback.\n- Use the credentials only for HTTP Basic auth against the **user-configured `JIRA_BASE_URL`** (`/rest/api/3/...`). No hardcoded hosts, no third-party endpoints, no exfiltration, no obfuscation, no remote-code execution, no filesystem writes outside what you'd expect.\n\n**What I deliberately did NOT execute against a real target:** the `demo`/`start`/`complete`/`reopen`/`batch-*` commands perform real `POST` transitions and add comments \342\200\224 these are account-affecting and effectively irreversible. No real Jira instance or credentials are configured in this sandbox, so I exercised the identical network code path safely against an unreachable localhost port instead.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skill_name\": \"jira-transitions\",\n  \"documented_purpose\": \"Move Jira issues through workflow states (To Do / In Progress / Done), query available transitions, set resolutions, and bulk-transition via the Atlassian Jira Cloud REST API v3.\",\n  \"files_inspected\": [\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/jira-transitions/SKILL.md\",\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/jira-transitions/scripts/workflow-demo.mjs\",\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/jira-transitions/scripts/workflow-demo.py\"\n  ],\n  \"commands_executed\": [\n    \"ls -la (skill dir + scripts dir)\",\n    \"node --version  -> v18.20.8\",\n    \"python3 --ve"..., 5567) = 5567
